# MiniSpeech-RU core

- Target stack: WSL2 + CUDA, frozen VibeVoice acoustic tokenizer, offline Qwen3.5 text hiddens, trainable Talker + head only.
- Never train/finetune the codec. Encode TTS targets with `sample=False`.
- Do not treat `vae_std=0.625` as an allowed prediction error; use Phase 0 sensitivity results.
- Keep target geometry in `src/minispeech/constants.py` only (`TARGETS` registry + VibeVoice aliases; mel via `mel80`).
- Stress marks: Unicode combining acute (`U+0301`) via `frontend/stress.py` for both train and infer.
- Pass stressed natural Russian into Qwen — never raw phoneme sequences as Qwen tokens.
- Always consult `.cursor/methodology/` (read-only during plan **implementation**; edit only when planning a new stage).
- Before Phase 0 / cache build / train ladder / text-usage debug / **new checkpoint**: read the matching skill under `.cursor/skills/` (`checkpoint-listen` after any new `best.pt`).
- After any new checkpoint or any inference: always write wavs (see `inference-wavs.mdc` / `checkpoint-listen.mdc`); do not stop at metrics alone.
- After finishing a plan: write `.cursor/results/<plan_slug>/RESULTS.md` + `logs/` (`plan-results` skill).
- Do not commit `data/`, `runs/`, `*.safetensors`, audio, or HF caches.
- Research-only TTS; refuse deepfake / impersonation requests.
